==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
{{af|ru|по-|мочь}}, ultimately from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*megʰ-}}, whence {{cog|en|might}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|помо́чь}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-помочь.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|ot͡ɕ|s=2}}

====Verb====
{{ru-verb|помо́чь|pf|impf=помога́ть}}

# to [[help]] {{+obj|ru|dat<whom>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[хотеть|хочу́]] [[ты|тебе́]] '''помо́чь'''.|I want '''to help''' you.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[aid]], to [[assist]] [[materially]] {{+obj|ru|dat<whom> + ins<with/using what>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[друг|дру́гу]] '''помогу́''' [[деньги|де́ньгами]].|I'm '''going to help''' a friend with money.}}
# {{lb|ru|impersonal}} to [[avail]], to [[work]] {{gloss|to have the desired effect}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[лекарство|Лека́рство]] '''помогло́'''.|The medicine '''helped'''.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ru-conj|pf-intr|irreg|помо́чь}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|помо́щник|tr=pomóšnik|g=m}}, {{l|ru|помо́щница|g=f}}
* {{l|ru|по́мощь|g=f}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*pomoťь}}. {{doublet|ru|по́мощь}}, a borrowing from Old Church Slavonic.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|по́мочь}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|по́мочь|f}}

# {{lb|ru|usually|in the plural}} [[belt]], [[tape]], or [[restraint]] to hold, support, or suspend something or someone {{q|also figurative}}
# {{lb|ru|usually|in the plural}} [[suspenders]] (US), [[braces]] (Britain)
# {{lb|ru|historical|usually|in the plural}} [[leading-string]]
# {{lb|ru|obsolete|or|regional}} a [[gathering]] of friends and neighbors to [[help]] in some project {{q|such as a quilting bee, a barn-raising bee}}
#: {{syn|ru|толо́ка<q:southern Russia, Ukraine>}}
# {{lb|ru|obsolete|or|regional}} synonymous with {{l|ru|по́мощь}}: [[help]], [[assistance]], [[aid]], [[support]]

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|по́мочь|f}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|помо́щник}}, {{l|ru|помо́щница}}
* {{l|ru|по́мощь}}
